                <pb facs="0213" n="139" sameAs="frus:frus1866p2/pg139"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. King to Mr.
                        Seward.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#float-left">No. 62.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-08-08"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >August</hi> 8, 1866</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> * * * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I availed myself of the opportunity to repeat to the cardinal the information
                    communicated to me by St. Marie in regard to John H. Surratt. His Eminence was
                    greatly interested by it, and intimated that if the American government desired
                    the surrender of the criminal there would probably be no difficulty in the
                    way.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUEUS KING.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
